.TH VLC-AUTO-RESUME-ENABLE 1 "November 2026" "vlc-auto-resume" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vlc-auto-resume-enable \- configure VLC for the auto-resume Lua interface extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vlc-auto-resume-enable
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vlc-auto-resume-enable
configures the current user's VLC Media Player configuration file
.RI ( ~/.config/vlc/vlcrc )
to activate the system-wide
.B vlc-auto-resume
Lua interface extension.
.PP
Specifically, the helper performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Unlocks
.I ~/.config/vlc/vlcrc
if it was previously set to read-only.
.IP \(bu 2
Enables the
.B luaintf
interface module and sets
.B lua-intf=vlc-auto-resume
so VLC tracks playback positions for local files and UPnP/DLNA streams.
.IP \(bu 2
Sets
.B qt-continue=0
to disable VLC's built-in Qt resume prompt, preventing duplicate dialogs on startup.
.IP \(bu 2
Locks
.I ~/.config/vlc/vlcrc
with read-only permissions
.RI ( 0444 )
so VLC does not overwrite the Lua interface settings on exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vlc/vlcrc
Per-user VLC configuration file modified and locked by this utility.
.TP
.I /usr/share/vlc/lua/intf/vlc-auto-resume.lua
System-wide VLC Lua interface script invoked when VLC starts.
.SH NOTES
Because VLC reads
.I vlcrc
at startup and rewrites it on exit, the configuration file is locked read-only after updating. To change VLC preferences later via the GUI, temporarily restore write permissions with
.B chmod u+w ~/.config/vlc/vlcrc
before launching VLC, then run
.B vlc-auto-resume-enable
again afterward.
